# Soil Moisture-Based Plant Watering Alert System

## Description
An Arduino-based plant monitoring system that uses a soil moisture sensor to 
detect when soil becomes too dry. When moisture drops below a set threshold, 
an LED and buzzer alert the user that the plant needs watering.

## Components Used
- Arduino Uno R3
- Soil Moisture Sensor
- LED
- Buzzer

## Circuit Connections
| Component | Arduino Pin |
|-----------|-------------|
| Soil Moisture Sensor (OUT) | Analog Pin A0 |
| LED (+) | Digital Pin 7 |
| Buzzer (+) | Digital Pin 8 |

## How It Works
1. The soil moisture sensor continuously reads the moisture level of the soil.
2. The analog value is printed to the Serial Monitor every second.
3. If the reading falls below the threshold (dry soil), the LED and buzzer 
   turn ON to alert that watering is needed.
4. If the soil is sufficiently moist, the LED and buzzer stay OFF.

